.TITLE "cat"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Concatenates and displays file content. It reads data from files or standard input and writes it to the terminal or redirects it to another location.

.DIV "TLDR"
**cat file.txt**
Prints the entire contents of a file to the terminal.
> __file.txt__ the source file

**cat -n file.txt**
Displays the file contents with line numbers.
> __-n__ number lines flag

**cat source.txt > destination.txt**
Copies the content of one file into another using redirection.
> __source.txt__ source file | __>__ redirection | __destination.txt__ target file

**cat file1.txt file2.txt > combined.txt**
Joins the contents of multiple files into a single new file.
> __file1.txt__ first file | __file2.txt__ second file | __combined.txt__ output file

.DIV "SUMMARY"
While __cat__ is excellent for short files, tools like __less__ or __more__ are better suited for reading long documents as they allow for scrolling and searching.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
